    "state": "open",
    "locked": false,
    "maintainer_can_modify": true,
    "title": "mining: avoid checkBlock crash when chain has no tip",
    "user": {
      "login": "danielabrozzoni",
      "id": 25042473,
      "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjI1MDQyNDcz",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25042473?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/danielabrozzoni",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/danielabrozzoni",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/danielabrozzoni/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/danielabrozzoni/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/danielabrozzoni/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/danielabrozzoni/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/danielabrozzoni/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/danielabrozzoni/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/danielabrozzoni/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/danielabrozzoni/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/danielabrozzoni/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "**The problem**: `Init.makeMining` returns as soon as the chainstate is loaded. On a first start with an empty datadir, or on a node started with `-reindex`/`-reindex-chainstate`, this is before the genesis block is connected, so the active chain has no tip. A `Mining.checkBlock` call in this window reaches `TestBlockValidity()`, which asserts that the tip exists, and the node aborts.\n\n**The fix**: In `Mining.checkBlock`, check if the tip is present, return early with \"inconclusive-no-chain-tip\" otherwise. \n\n**Alternative fix**: We already have a `wait_loaded` parameter in `MakeMining`, implemented in #34661, which could be expanded to also wait for the tip to be connected. I don't feel strongly about this solution over the one I already implemented, looking for feedback here :)\n\nThe crash can be reproduced on master using this functional test: https://github.com/danielabrozzoni/bitcoin/commit/270211a70d07f256aead2631dafa264b16ceeaab (It's not included in the PR as it might be flaky, so I decided to introduce a unit test instead)\n\nThis is joint work with Turtlecute33 :)",
