          "html_url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/commit/e211dd0186e9646167d063a16f0da88e5f72e05f"
        }
      ],
      "message": "mining: avoid checkBlock crash when chain has no tip\n\n`Init.makeMining` returns as soon as the chainstate is loaded. On a first\nstart with an empty datadir, or on a node started with\n`reindex/reindex-chainstate`, this is before the genesis block is\nconnected, so the active chain has no tip. A `Mining.checkBlock` call in\nthis window reaches `TestBlockValidity()`, which asserts that the tip\nexists, and the node aborts.\n\nFix it by checking if the tip is present, return early with\n\"inconclusive-no-chain-tip\" otherwise.\n\nCo-authored-by: Daniela Brozzoni <danielabrozzoni@protonmail.com>",
      "committer": {
        "name": "Daniela Brozzoni",
        "email": "danielabrozzoni@protonmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-18T00:47:48Z"
